# P2-03 (v2.1.0 third code review round): this file did not exist before
# this fix. Its absence is exactly how the delivered v2.1.0.dev0 release
# archive ended up containing test-run cache/state directories nobody
# intended to ship -- 165 of that archive's 356 files (.hypothesis/,
# .import_linter_cache/, and friends) were pytest/hypothesis/mypy/ruff/
# import-linter scratch state, not source. See scripts/package_release.sh,
# which now builds the release archive from an explicit include list (never
# a bare "tar up the whole directory") specifically so this cannot recur
# even if a step here is ever missed -- but this file is still the honest,
# conventional signal to anyone (a person, `git status`, an editor) working
# in this tree of what is source and what is disposable, independent of the
# packaging script itself.

# Python bytecode / package build artifacts
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
dist/
build/

# Test, type-check and lint state (regenerated by every run; never source)
.pytest_cache/
.hypothesis/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.import_linter_cache/
htmlcov/
.coverage
.coverage.*

# Virtual environments
.venv/
venv/

# This project uses constraints.txt as its tested dependency-resolution record.
# Do not accidentally add a separately generated resolver state with different
# semantics.
uv.lock

# Scratch SQLite/cache-db files a local run may create at the repo root
# (the CLI's --sqlite-path/--cache-db/--sealed-store flags all default to
# caller-chosen paths, never anything under version control, but a
# developer experimenting from the repo root can easily land one here)
*.db
*.sqlite3

# Editor/OS cruft
.DS_Store
*.swp
